WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.576 --> 00:00:05.418
Henry hurried toward Nora, who was huddled against the tree.

2
00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.519
"What are you doing over there?"

3
00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:07.919
he asked.

4
00:00:07.999 --> 00:00:09.500
"None of your business!"

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.461
Nora cried, looking upset.

6
00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:15.023
"Do you guys hear something?"

7
00:00:15.043 --> 00:00:17.224
Maggie asked.

8
00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.465
A high-pitched sound was coming from the tree trunk.

9
00:00:35.465 --> 00:00:38.166
At first Henry thought it was an insect or a frog.

10
00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:40.527
Then he heard it again.

11
00:00:40.547 --> 00:00:43.667
"It sounds like—," he began.

12
00:00:43.687 --> 00:00:46.508
"Kittens!" Maggie cried.

13
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.331
there's a mother cat and a bunch of adorable kittens!"

14
00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:58.552
Nora burst into tears.

15
00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:01.510
"Please don't tell anyone!"

16
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:02.530
She sobbed.

17
00:01:04.172 --> 00:01:10.117
"If Mom and Dad find out, they'll take Patches and her babies to the shelter!

18
00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:14.180
They said I couldn't have any pets!"

19
00:01:15.021 --> 00:01:16.302
Henry glanced at his friends.

20
00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:20.345
He remembered what Nathan had told them about Nora wanting a pet.

21
00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:25.469
She must have found this cat and her kittens and decided to take care of them in secret.

22
00:01:25.489 --> 00:01:28.692
"It's okay, Nora," Maggie said.

23
00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:33.495
"We'll make sure nothing bad happens to Patches and her kittens.

24
00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:35.276
I promise."

25
00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:38.359
"Really?" Nora wiped her eyes.

26
00:01:38.379 --> 00:01:43.343
"Really." Maggie reached in and tickled a kitten under its chin.

27
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:45.985
"Aw, they're so cute!"

28
00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.148
"Come on, Nora," Henry said.

29
00:01:49.168 --> 00:01:51.490
"We'd better get you home."

30
00:01:55.793 --> 00:01:58.516
The next day Henry met Cole at the lemonade stand.

31
00:02:00.172 --> 00:02:00.893
"Where's Maggie?"

32
00:02:01.173 --> 00:02:01.913
Cole asked.

33
00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:04.255
"I was hoping for some lemonade."

34
00:02:04.275 --> 00:02:07.197
"She'll be here soon," Henry said.

35
00:02:07.217 --> 00:02:12.040
"She offered to walk over to Nathan's house to pick up our five-dollar fee."

36
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.283
"Cool! I already know how I'm going to spend my share."

37
00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.404
Cole grinned.

38
00:02:18.424 --> 00:02:22.367
"I want glow-in-the-dark laces for my soccer shoes."

39
00:02:22.387 --> 00:02:26.950
"We definitely earned our fee this time," Henry said.

40
00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.452
"That was a tricky case!

41
00:02:30.568 --> 00:02:33.810
At least now we know why Nora sneaked out mostly at night.

42
00:02:34.911 --> 00:02:38.412
She didn't want anyone to see her carrying cans of tuna into the woods."

43
00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:40.193
Cole nodded.

44
00:02:40.213 --> 00:02:42.174
"I feel sorry for her.

45
00:02:43.695 --> 00:02:46.097
She seemed really upset about losing her new pets."

46
00:02:46.117 --> 00:02:50.059
"Actually she's not losing them," Henry said.

47
00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:52.600
"I talked to Nathan this morning.

48
00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:56.862
He said his parents aren't against having a pet after all."

49
00:02:57.983 --> 00:02:59.784
"Really?" Cole looked surprised.

50
00:03:00.696 --> 00:03:03.277
"But Nathan said they told Nora she couldn't have one!"

51
00:03:03.297 --> 00:03:07.499
"That was a year ago," Henry reminded him.

52
00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:11.360
"They didn't think she was ready to take care of a pet then.

53
00:03:12.521 --> 00:03:13.581
But she's older now.

54
00:03:14.682 --> 00:03:18.543
They said if she promised to be good from now on, she could keep Patches.

55
00:03:19.644 --> 00:03:22.205
And Patches' kittens can stay until someone adopts them."

56
00:03:23.105 --> 00:03:24.646
"Awesome!" Cole said.

57
00:03:25.626 --> 00:03:26.947
Then he pointed down the street.

58
00:03:26.967 --> 00:03:29.268
"Here comes Maggie with our money.

59
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.840
That's even more awesome!"

60
00:03:33.521 --> 00:03:36.582
Maggie hurried over, carrying a plate covered in foil.

61
00:03:36.602 --> 00:03:39.142
"Hi, guys," she said.

62
00:03:39.162 --> 00:03:41.203
"Ready to sell more lemonade?

63
00:03:42.043 --> 00:03:43.404
I'll run inside and get the pitchers."

64
00:03:44.444 --> 00:03:46.484
"First things first," Cole said.

65
00:03:46.504 --> 00:03:48.765
"Did you get our fee from Nathan?"

66
00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:50.065
Maggie hesitated.

67
00:03:50.085 --> 00:03:52.846
"Um, sort of."

68
00:03:52.866 --> 00:03:55.427
"What do you mean, sort of?"

69
00:03:55.907 --> 00:03:56.527
Henry said.

70
00:03:58.008 --> 00:03:59.328
Maggie smiled sheepishly.

71
00:04:00.384 --> 00:04:03.205
"Did you notice how adorable those kittens were?"

72
00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:06.586
"Yeah, they were cute," Cole said impatiently.

73
00:04:06.606 --> 00:04:08.606
"But where's my money?

74
00:04:09.586 --> 00:04:10.807
Did Nathan pay you or not?"

75
00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:13.988
"He paid me," Maggie said.

76
00:04:14.008 --> 00:04:15.928
"But not with money.

77
00:04:15.948 --> 00:04:21.050
I, um, told him I'd take two kittens instead of the five dollars."

78
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.711
"What?" Cole shrieked.

79
00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:26.711
"Are you kidding?"

80
00:04:26.731 --> 00:04:29.892
"Sorry," Maggie said quickly.

81
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.141
"I know I should have checked with you guys first.

82
00:04:33.201 --> 00:04:38.824
But the kittens are so cute, and they need homes I just couldn't resist, even if it means

83
00:04:38.885 --> 00:04:40.605
waiting longer to start riding lessons."

84
00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:42.747
Cole looked annoyed.

85
00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:48.090
"Okay, you got two kittens for solving the case," he complained.

86
00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.371
"What do Henry and I get?"

87
00:04:50.391 --> 00:04:55.134
"You can split our next detective fee, just the two of you," Maggie said.

88
00:04:55.154 --> 00:04:56.995
"I promise."

89
00:04:58.195 --> 00:04:58.996
Henry smiled.

90
00:05:00.112 --> 00:05:03.294
It hadn't been fair for Maggie to give away their fee without asking.

91
00:05:04.715 --> 00:05:08.417
But if she was willing to give up her share of the next one, she must really want

92
00:05:08.457 --> 00:05:09.097
those kittens.

93
00:05:09.117 --> 00:05:13.119
"It's a deal," he said before Cole could respond.

94
00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:17.202
"Great!" Maggie seemed relieved.

95
00:05:17.222 --> 00:05:21.524
"And look, Nathan's mom gave us these to thank us!"

96
00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:23.965
She uncovered the plate.

97
00:05:24.946 --> 00:05:26.747
It was full of chocolate chip cookies.

98
00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:31.249
"Yum." That made Cole a little happier.

99
00:05:31.269 --> 00:05:34.290
"Just ask next time, Maggie, okay?"

100
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:35.991
Maggie nodded.

101
00:05:36.011 --> 00:05:43.073
"Sorry." Meanwhile Henry had spotted Gail and her older sister walking toward them.

102
00:05:43.093 --> 00:05:45.534
"Uh-oh," he said.

103
00:05:45.554 --> 00:05:48.976
"I think our first customers of the day are coming.

104
00:05:50.396 --> 00:05:51.497
We'd better get some lemonade."

105
00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.298
"Be right back."

106
00:05:54.318 --> 00:05:58.860
Maggie dashed into the house and returned a few seconds later carrying two pitchers of lemonade.

107
00:06:00.768 --> 00:06:03.190
By then the girls had reached the lemonade stand.

108
00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:07.093
"Two lemonades please," Gail's sister said.

109
00:06:07.113 --> 00:06:11.257
"We heard you solved another case," Gail added.

110
00:06:11.277 --> 00:06:13.939
"You heard about that already?"

111
00:06:14.319 --> 00:06:15.440
Cole looked excited.

112
00:06:16.521 --> 00:06:18.283
The three friends grinned at each other.

113
00:06:19.404 --> 00:06:22.726
Henry was glad that word was spreading about The Lemonade Detectives.

114
00:06:23.847 --> 00:06:25.349
That would bring them more cases.

115
00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.972
He couldn't wait to find out what the next one would be!
